{
  "summary": "This study investigates how dual twisted interfaces in CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 affect second harmonic generation (SHG). By fabricating nine distinct stacking configurations, the researchers analyzed Raman and photoluminescence data to show that interlayer coupling varies with stacking. Atomic-resolution imaging confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice. They developed a framework linking interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization, demonstrating TT-MoS2 as a tunable nonlinear optical platform.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 with dual twisted interfaces exhibits stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses",
    "Atomic-resolution techniques confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice structure",
    "A framework was established linking dual interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization orientation"
  ],
  "study_type": "CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 with nine distinct stacking configurations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational understanding of multi-interface twisted coupling in van der Waals materials, enabling precise engineering of nonlinear optical responses through interface geometry."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei to construct a comprehensive atlas of regulatory elements. It combined histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization to define 100+ cell subclasses and assign chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define repressive states. The resource enables deep learning models for predicting epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequences.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Integration of four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome data across 2.5 million mouse brain nuclei",
    "Active chromatin states defined by combinatorial histone modifications more accurately predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct repressive mechanisms for cell-type-specific gene silencing"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell epigenomic profiling",
  "scientific_significance": "This atlas provides a unified framework for annotating brain regulatory elements and interpreting non-coding disease variants through cell-type-specific epigenomic features."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how circumventricular organs (CVOs) function as immune niches influencing brain macrophage development. Van Hove et al. demonstrate that CVOs generate specialized macrophage phenotypes and enable fetal monocytes to adopt microglial identities through local tissue context. The findings reveal CVOs as critical regulators of immune cell fate in the brain.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CVOs act as distinct immune niches shaping brain macrophage identity",
    "Fetal monocytes adopt microglial identities within CVOs",
    "Local tissue context determines immune cell fate specification"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes circumvent: CVOs as key regulators of macrophage differentiation and immune cell fate in the central nervous system, providing mechanistic insights into brain immune cell development."
  }

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of creating interactive graphical user interfaces (GUIs) compatible with textiles by developing a digital pixel fibre. The approach integrates addressable pixels, interconnections, and touch-sensing layers into a single fibre. The resulting garment sleeve GUI achieves a 96×54-pixel display with 30fps refresh rate and :8-bit color, supporting dynamic graphics, audio-video playback, and wireless data exchange while maintaining textile flexibility and durability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Digital pixel fibres integrate addressable pixels, interconnections, and touch-sensing layers for textile-compatible GUIs",
    "The system achieves a 96×54-pixel display with 30 frames per second refresh rate and 8-bit color depth",
    "Garments with this technology support dynamic graphics, audio-video playback, and wireless data exchange while retaining textile properties"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable platform for intrinsically interactive textiles, enabling garments to function as fully integrated computational systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluates cellular agriculture's potential for sustainable food production by analyzing enabling technologies, food functionality, and manufacturing economics. It identifies that precision fermentation should prioritize functional improvements in taste, nutrition, and health rather than direct food imitation, while cultivated meat benefits from hybrid products that avoid full tissue mimicry costs. The field is nearing an inflection point where scalable, affordable manufacturing becomes more critical than biological technology development for commercial viability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Precision fermentation should focus on functional enhancements like taste and nutritional quality rather than direct food imitation",
    "Cultivated meat production can achieve cost efficiency through hybrid products that avoid full tissue mimicry",
    "Scalable, affordable manufacturing processes are now more critical for commercial success than biological technology development"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that cellular agriculture's transition to commercial viability hinges on optimizing manufacturing economics and functional product design rather than further biological innovation, shifting the focus from technological development to scalable production systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how autophagy in alveolar macroinflammation regulates innate immune priming against respiratory pathogens. Using genetic manipulation of autophagy in macrophages, researchers found autophagy suppresses IL-1α expression, thereby maintaining protective innate immune responses to Staphylococcus aureus and influenza A virus. Autophagy deficiency enhanced IL-1α-mediated neutrophil recruitment and reduced pathogen clearance efficiency, indicating autophagy's role in balancing immune activation during early infection responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Autophagy suppression in alveolar macrophages reduces IL-1α expression",
    "Autophagy deficiency increases IL-1α-mediated neutrophil recruitment",
    "Autophagy loss impairs clearance of Staphylococcus aureus and influenza A virus"
  ],
  "study_type": "Genetic manipulation of autophagy in alveolar macrophages",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes autophagy as a critical regulator of innate immune priming against respiratory infections by modulating IL-1α expression, providing a mechanistic insight into balancing immune activation and pathogen clearance."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a process-intrinsic cellular network in a 3D-printed Cr-Fe-Co-Ni-Al-Ti-based multi-principal element alloy (MPEA) to achieve sustained strength-ductility across temperatures. Using laser-based additive manufacturing, the researchers designed a (CrFeCo)48Ni34Al7Ti5V5Ta1 MPEA with a self-assembled body-centred cubic/L21 precipitate network. This network enables slip transfer and back-stress hardening across specific interfaces, stabilizing deformation from 77 to 873 K. The alloy maintains yield strength above 1 GPa and uniform elongation of ~20% over this temperature range, demonstrating stable mechanical performance without post-processing.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A self-assembled body-centred cubic/L21 precipitate cellular network forms intrinsically during laser-based additive manufacturing.",
    "Slip transfer and back-stress hardening across Kurdjumov-Sachs and Nishiyama-Wassermann interfaces stabilize deformation from 77 to 873 K.",
    "The alloy maintains yield strength >1 GPa and uniform elongation of ~20% across a wide temperature range without post-processing."
  ],
  "study_type": "Laser-based additive manufacturing (LAM)",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a process-intrinsic pathway for designing strong, ductile alloys with reduced temperature sensitivity through interface-mediated plasticity mechanisms in additive manufacturing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses reduced power conversion efficiency and stability in flexible perovskite solar modules due to surface hydroxyls disrupting self-assembled monolayer anchoring. By decoupling SAM-perovskite deposition, the researchers accelerated SAM anchoring and improved perov. The certified PCE reached 20.2% on 750 cm² devices, with 22.0% efficiency on smaller devices showing 8% degradation after 1044 hours at 85°C and 65% humidity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Decoupled SAM-perovskite codeposition strategy accelerates SAM anchoring by reducing SAM-perovskite interactions",
    "Certified power conversion efficiency of 20.2% achieved on 750 cm² flexible perovskite solar modules",
    "22.0% efficient devices retained 80% of initial efficiency after 1044 hours under 85°C and 65% humidity"
  ],
  "study_type": "Decoupled SAM-perovskite codeposition strategy",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach enhances the stability and efficiency of flexible perovskite solar modules by mitigating surface hydroxyl-induced degradation, providing a pathway to commercialize high-performance portable photovoltaic devices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how NAD+ acts as a metabolic signal to maintain an epigenetic mark critical for trained immunity by suppressing the histone demethylase KDM5a. The research demonstrates that NAD+ preserves this mark through inhibition of KDM5a, thereby supporting innate immune memory. The findings suggest NAD+ plays a key role in metabolic licensing of innate immune memory.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NAD+ inhibits histone demethylase KDM5a to preserve an epigenetic mark for trained immunity",
    "NAD+ serves as a metabolic signal maintaining innate immune memory",
    "KDM5a suppression by NAD+ is central to metabolic licensing of innate immune memory"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes NAD+ as a critical metabolic regulator that sustains epigenetic mechanisms underlying innate immune memory, advancing understanding of how metabolic signals license immune memory."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the research redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and enhances Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with reduced expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect expansion stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The design reduces electrode thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables scalable production"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro engineering study",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, addressing critical mechanical and electrochemical instability in high-energy lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how stromal PD-L1 expression influences germinal center (GC) dynamics and humoral immunity. Using in vitro and in vivo models, researchers found that PD-L1 on stromal cells promotes T-B cell interactions and GC responses. The results indicate PD-L:1's role in sustaining GC activity through stromal interactions, with implications for immune regulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PD-L1 on stromal cells enhances T-B cell collaboration",
    "PD-L1 expression supports germinal center maintenance",
    "PD-L1 regulates humoral immunity via stromal interactions"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work clarifies a critical mechanism by which stromal cells modulate germinal center responses through PD-L1, advancing understanding of immune regulation pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether root cell lineages in Arabidopsis exhibit environmental plasticity. Using single-cell RNA sequencing and spatial transcript mapping, researchers discovered that most root cell lineages follow a stereotyped bifid topology. One branch shows a transcriptional program enriched for environmental response genes, including ABA signaling. This state is reproducible across cell types, conserved across ecotypes, and modulated by water deficit conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Most Arabidopsis root cell lineages display a stereotyped bifid topology",
    "One branch of the lineage exhibits a transcriptional program enriched for environmental response genes, including ABA signaling",
    "This state is conserved across Arabidopsis ecotypes and modulated by water deficit conditions"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings reveal an environmentally regulated layer of root cell identity that operates independently of developmental lineage, providing new insights into how environmental cues shape cellular heterogeneity in plant roots."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluates the deployability of 77 biotechnologies across eight agricultural domains using a Balanced Readiness Level framework assessing technological, market, regulatory, acceptance, and organizational factors. Findings indicate market viability and social acceptance are primary constraints, with high-readiness technologies being 'drop-in', contained, and perceived as natural. The research suggests strategies to enhance deployability, such as improving GMO containment, and proposes a roadmap for ecosystem-level biological systems to boost food security and environmental resilience.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Market viability and social acceptance, not technological readiness, are the main barriers to biotechnology deployability",
    "High-readiness biotechnologies are characterized as 'drop-in', contained, and perceived as natural",
    "Strategies to improve deployability include addressing GMO containment and developing ecosystem-level biological systems"
  ],
  "study_type": "Balanced Readiness Level assessment",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a systematic framework for evaluating biotechnology deployability across multiple environmental and societal dimensions, advancing understanding of how to integrate biotechnologies into resilient agricultural systems without compromising ecological or social sustainability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how tumor tissue stiffness impacts TH1 cell function in pancreatic cancer. Using mechanotransduction analysis, researchers found stiffness activates YAP-RUNX1 signaling, reprogramming TH1 cells to suppress antitumor immunity via M2 macrophage polarization. Inhibition of YAP-Rusing this pathway reversed immunosuppression, suggesting a targetable mechanism for enhancing immunotherapy in stiff tumors.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Elevated tissue stiffness reprograms TH1 cells through YAP-RUNX1 signaling",
    "Reprogrammed TH1 cells secrete factors promoting M2 macrophage polarization",
    "YAP inhibition restores antitumor immunity by reversing TH1 dysfunction"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo mechanotransduction analysis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a direct mechanobiological link between tumor stiffness and immunosuppression, providing a novel targetable pathway to overcome resistance to immunotherapies in mechanically stiff cancers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the optical spin Hall effect in WS2-based polariton waveguides by coupling bright and dark excitons with photonic modes. Non-resonant pumping populates dark excitons, generating transverse-magnetic and transverse-electric polariton modes with out-of-plane electric fields. The research demonstrates eight polarization domains and spin-polarized currents propagating 92 ± 1 μm at room temperature, enabling room-temperature spin-optoelectronic applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Observation of eight polarization domains via optical spin Hall effect in WS2 polariton waveguides",
    "Spin-polarized polariton currents propagating up to 92 ± 1 μm at room temperature",
    "Dark excitons feed both transverse-magnetic and transverse-electric polariton modes under non-resonant pumping"
  ],
  "study_type": "Exciton-polariton waveguide",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes transition metal dichalcogenide polariton waveguides as a viable room-temperature platform for spin-optoelectronic devices through the demonstration of robust spin-polarized currents and domain formation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the editorial selection process in Science journal, analyzing how editors curate high-impact publications. The research identifies patterns in selection criteria and the role of editorial judgment in determining which articles receive prominent coverage. Findings indicate that editorial decisions prioritize scientific novelty and broad relevance, though the process remains subjective and influenced by multiple factors.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Editors prioritize scientific novelty and broad relevance in selecting high-impact publications",
    "The editorial selection process involves subjective judgment influenced by multiple factors",
    "Patterns in selection criteria reveal a focus on articles with significant scientific contributions"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides insight into the mechanisms of high-impact publication curation, highlighting how editorial decisions balance scientific merit with broader scientific discourse."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether bystander T cells can eliminate tumors without recognizing specific antigens. Using in vitro models, researchers observed that T cells from healthy donors could destroy tumor cells even without antigen engagement. The findings suggest a potential mechanism for tumor eradication independent of antigen-specific recognition, though the exact pathways remain unclear.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Bystander T cells destroy tumor cells without antigen recognition",
    "T cells from healthy donors eliminate tumor targets in vitro",
    "Tumor eradication occurs independently of antigen-specific engagement"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro models",
  "scientific_significance": "This work reveals a novel tumor-eradication mechanism that operates without antigen-specific T cell recognition, expanding understanding of immune responses beyond conventional antigen-driven pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates an additive-free photocatalyst for H2O2 synthesis using hollow conjugated microporous polymers (hPSe) anchored with ZnxCd1-xS quantum dots (QDs). The S-scheme heterojunction enhances charge separation and light harvesting, achieving a high H2O2 production rate of 15.13 mmol g-1 h-1 via 2e- ORR in pure water without sacrificial agents.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Achieved 15.13 mmol g-1 h-1 H2O2 production rate in pure water without sacrificial agents",
    "S-scheme charge transfer mechanism preserved strong redox potentials and suppressed bulk recombination",
    "Synergy factor of 1.53 and apparent quantum efficiency of 8.82% at 400 nm"
  ],
  "study_type": "In situ growth of ZnxCd1-xS quantum dots on hollow conjugated microporous polymers",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a rational design strategy for efficient additive-free photocatalysts through S-scheme heterojunctions, advancing sustainable H2O2 production via 2e- ORR without sacrificial reagents."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the mechanisms underlying allergic relapse in human skin. Researchers identified a pathogenic CXCR6+ subset of skin-resident memory CD4+ T cells that persists despite biologic treatment in atopic dermatitis. The findings suggest these cells may drive recurrent allergic inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CXCR6+ skin-resident memory CD4+ T cells persist after biologic treatment in atopic dermatitis",
    "These cells are pathogenic and contribute to allergic relapse",
    "They represent a target for preventing recurrent allergic inflammation"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery of CXCR6+ skin-resident memory CD4+ T cells provides insight into the persistence of allergic inflammation post-treatment, potentially informing strategies to prevent relapse in atopic dermatitis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates functional heterogeneity among astrocytes using a CD51-FLP mouse model to compare CD51+ and CD51- subpopulations. It demonstrates distinct morphological, physiological, and developmental properties in cortex and hippocampus. CD51+ astrocytes promote cortical synapse formation and hippocampal circuit plasticity, with CD51 acting via glypican 6 for synapses and driving plasticity. These subtypes also aid stroke recovery through synaptic remodelling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CD51+ astrocytes selectively promote synapse formation in developing cortex",
    "CD51+ astrocytes drive hippocampal circuit plasticity",
    "CD51+ astrocytes enhance functional recovery after stroke via synaptic remodelling"
  ],
  "study_type": "CD51-FLP mouse model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies functionally distinct astrocyte subtypes with specialized roles in neural development, plasticity, and injury recovery, advancing understanding of astrocyte heterogeneity in brain physiology."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. ILC3s in healthy human guts express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or inflammatory bowel disease, indicating PKA signaling's role in maintaining gut immune balance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion in mice reduced ILC3s and increased enteric infection susceptibility",
    "ILC3s in healthy human guts express PRKAR1A, downregulated by IL-23 or inflammatory bowel disease"
  ],
  "study_type": "single-cell atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive gut inflammation through PRKAR1A-mediated mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how nanoparticle superlattices can achieve lower symmetry and coordination numbers without particle anisotropy. Using flexible electrostatically active nanoparticles, the researchers demonstrate that ligand coronas reconfigure during assembly to create effective valency. The findings reveal that increasing ligand deformability reduces lattice coordination and packing density, enabling programmable assembly of isotropic particles into less symmetric structures than hard-sphere models predict.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ligand coronas reconfigure during assembly to generate effective valency",
    "Increasing ligand deformability lowers lattice coordination numbers",
    "Assemblies achieve lower symmetry and packing density than hard-sphere predictions"
  ],
  "study_type": "Experimental and simulation",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes ligand flexibility as a fundamental design parameter for programming coordination in nanoparticle superlattices, advancing the field beyond geometric constraints."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether advanced language models could effectively perform sequential diagnosis, mimicking iterative clinical reasoning. The researchers created an interactive benchmark and an AI system simulating physicians who iteratively refine differential diagnoses and select cost-effective tests. The model achieved 83.2% accuracy on NEJM conference cases and 80.3% on MIMIC-IV-ED admissions, surpassing generalist physicians' performance (36.1% and 46.8%, respectively). These results suggest language models hold potential for improving diagnostic accuracy while reducing costs in clinical settings.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The AI system achieved 83.2% accuracy on NEJM clinicopathological conference cases",
    "The model attained 80.3% accuracy on MIMIC-IV-ED emergency department admissions",
    "The system outperformed generalist physicians in both benchmarks (36.1% and 46.8%)"
  ],
  "study_type": "Interactive benchmark and AI system simulating physicians",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that language models can enhance diagnostic accuracy and reduce costs in clinical decision-making through iterative reasoning, offering a scalable approach to support more efficient healthcare diagnostics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how IL-36γ and IL-37 activate the IL-36 receptor (IL-36R) to drive proinflammatory signaling. Using cryo-EM, the researchers determined the structure of human IL-36γ bound to IL-36R and IL-1RAcP, revealing low-affinity engagement by IL-36γ that enables high-affinity IL-1RAcP recruitment. In contrast, IL-37 binds IL-36R with high affinity but weakly recruits IL-1RAcP. Functional assays confirmed both cytokines activate proinflammatory pathways, though IL-36γ shows significantly higher potency. The findings provide a structural basis for IL-36R activation mechanisms and spesolimab's allosteric antagonism.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-36γ binds IL-36R with low affinity but enables high-affinity IL-1RAcP recruitment",
    "IL-37 binds IL-36R with high affinity but recruits IL-1RAcP weakly",
    "IL-36γ exhibits markedly higher proinflammatory signaling potency than IL-37"
  ],
  "study_type": "Cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM) structure determination",
  "scientific_significance": "The structural insights clarify cytokine-specific activation mechanisms of IL-36R, advancing understanding of proinflammatory signaling complexity and therapeutic targeting strategies for skin inflammation."
}
